+## A turn that fails in beforeSession
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` is caught by the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: the rejection still reaches the caller unchanged, and `onError` fires for it with the session and the error ([validated by: fires onError with the session and the error, and the rejection still reaches the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L37)).
+- `afterSession` fires even when `beforeSession` threw, and the session it receives carries none of the turn — no user-input hook ran and no provider call was made — so a cleanup hook cannot assume any part of the turn happened ([validated by: runs afterSession after a failed beforeSession, for a session none of the turn has touched](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L60)).
+
